{
   // Typecheck configuration for CI.
   //
   // Two reasons the base tsconfig cannot be used directly with a bare
   // `tsc --noEmit`:
   //
   //   1. next-env.d.ts is generated by `next build` and is gitignored, so on a
   //      clean checkout it does not exist. It is what declares `*.png`,
   //      `*.jpeg` and friends as modules, and without it every
   //      `import img from "../public/assets/x.png"` is an error. The CI job
   //      writes the file before running tsc.
   //
   //   2. tests/ and cypress/ are listed in the base `include` and are stale -
   //      they import components that were removed (@/components/Button,
   //      @/components/parents/AuthLayout) and use jest-dom matchers whose
   //      types do not resolve. None of it ships. Blocking a deploy on a broken
   //      test file that nobody has run in a long time is noise, not safety.
   //
   // (2) is real tech debt worth fixing separately. Excluding it here makes CI
   // check the thing that actually gets built and served, which is the point.
   "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
   "exclude": [
      "node_modules",
      "**/*.jsx",
      "deploy",
      "tests",
      "cypress",
      "jest.config.js",
      "jest.setup.js"
   ]
}
